  "worked_solution": "A transformed reciprocal function of the form\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{a}{bx+c}+d\n$$\n\nhas the horizontal asymptote $y=d,$ and therefore, its range is\n\n$$\nf(x)\\in (-\\infty ,d)\\cup (d,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nIn our case, $d=1.$ Therefore, the horizontal asymptote is $y=1,$ and the range of the function is\n\n$$\nf(x)\\in (-\\infty ,1)\\cup (1,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nThe graph $y=f(x)$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14078796/assets/1a74169e0b8ed0494364e704ec742ed6a399f60db118a9506185c31ee61aaa80.png)",
